  "source_span": "So, let $s_k = b_1 + b_2 + \\dots + b_k.$  Using the recurrence $b_n = b_{n - 1} + 2b_{n - 2},$ we can compute the first few terms of $(b_n)$ and $(s_n)$ modulo 19:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|c|c}\nn & b_n & s_n \\\\ \\hline\n1 & 1 & 1 \\\\\n2 & 1 & 2 \\\\\n3 & 3 & 5 \\\\\n4 & 5 & 10 \\\\\n5 & 11 & 2 \\\\\n6 & 2 & 4 \\\\\n7 & 5 & 9 \\\\\n8 & 9 & 18 \\\\\n9 & 0 & 18 \\\\\n10 & 18 & 17 \\\\\n11 & 18 & 16 \\\\\n12 & 16 & 13 \\\\\n13 & 14 & 8 \\\\\n14 & 8 & 16 \\\\\n15 & 17 & 14 \\\\\n16 & 14 & 9 \\\\\n17 & 10 & 0\n\\end{array}\n\\]Thus, the smallest such $k$ is $\\boxed{17}.$",
